    "status": "present",
    "value": "Answer range queries with an element meeting threshold, or minus one; threshold is strictly greater than half the range length. The approach is: segment-tree Boyer-Moore candidates verified by exact indexed occurrence counts. Its target cost is build O(n), query O(log n), O(n) space; threshold strictly exceeds half. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
